Package: MrQAP
Title: Multiple Regression Quadratic Assignment Procedure for Networks
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Robert W.", "Krause",
      email = "robert.w.krause@uky.edu",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Estimates multiple regression quadratic assignment procedure
    (MRQAP) models on network matrices, on cognitive social structure (CSS)
    arrays, and on multi-mode data in which each dimension is its own node
    set. Supports gaussian, binomial, Poisson, negative binomial,
    zero-inflated Poisson and multinomial families with ordinary least
    squares, maximum likelihood and generalised method-of-moments
    estimators, optionally with fixed or random effects and
    heteroskedasticity-consistent standard errors. Permutation inference
    uses either Dekker's semi-partialling plus procedure, described in
    Dekker, Krackhardt and Snijders (2007) <doi:10.1007/s11336-007-9016-1>,
    or permutation of the outcome, following Krackhardt (1988)
    <doi:10.1016/0378-8733(88)90004-4>. Parallelisation is handled by the
    'future' framework, with optional GPU-accelerated batch estimation via
    'torch'.
